{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792311079,"nonce":"TwUO6oeviQvscUyRBAUwqdBGUq8=","title":"The generated page shows its console pane always; hide it unless debugging","message":"The page `ash --build` writes (crates/ash_page/page/index.html) lays out a `\u003cpre id=\"out\"\u003e` under the canvas, and a program that is an application, a window the user looks at, has the log below it. The user's direction: the pane is for debugging only; the browser's own console is where logs belong.\n\n**What is wanted**\n\n- `#out` is hidden by default and shown when the page is opened with `?debug` (a `hidden` attribute rather than leaving it out, so `document.getElementById(\"out\").textContent` still holds what the program wrote, which ashui's page runner reads).\n- The program's output keeps reaching the browser's console, as worker.js already does by wrapping `console.log` and `console.error`.\n- With the pane hidden, the canvas has the page to itself: not a 48 rem column with a margin, which crops a 1600 px window, and not `image-rendering: pixelated` for a GPU canvas that is not low resolution.\n\n**Where it is seen**\n\nashui's banner demo in headless Chrome: the canvas starts below a left margin and the log text sits under it.\n\n**Not asked**\n\nAny change to how a program may take over the page: removing the \"generated by ash\" line from index.html already stops it being rewritten.","files":null}]}